MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The screw, drill, tap and rivet gauge would help me identify and match parts in my screw and washer assortments, giving it a clear use alongside what I recently bought.",
    "The metric taps relate to my metric screws, and the casters connect with moving equipment, although I would need a threading task or a confirmed mounting fit before choosing them."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The wire connectors and clamp meter assume an electrical project that my recent fastener and magnetic-hook purchases do not establish.",
    "The disposable gloves do not solve my current hardware needs, while the resin printer introduces an activity I have shown no interest in pursuing."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations seem to treat workshop supplies as interchangeable, even though matching hardware, terminating wires and printing parts serve different purposes.",
    "Buying assorted screws and washers seems to have been taken as interest in other bulk supplies, but quantity alone does not make something useful to me."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent purchases point toward fastening, mounting and hanging things; tools that help identify or fit those parts have a clearer purpose for me.",
    "I rarely choose something without a specific use, and compatibility matters: metric sizes make the taps relevant, while the casters still need to fit the equipment I want to move."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly recognized my practical hardware interests but stretched them into unrelated electrical supplies, disposable gloves and a new hobby."
}
